{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"opposite-bicategory","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Opposite Bicategory"}]},"title_text":"Opposite Bicategory","kind":"definition","taxon":null,"url":"opposite-bicategory.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","opposite-bicategory"],["kind","definition"],["label","Definition"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"opposite"}]},{"Text":" "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)^\"op\""}},{"Text":" of a "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"bicategory","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"bicategory"}]}},{"Text":" "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)"}},{"Text":" has the same 0-cells and reverses the 1-cells but not the 2-cells:"}]},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)^\"op\"\n(x, y) = cal(B) (y, x) ."}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Composition swaps its arguments, "},{"Math":{"src":"f\n⋆^\"op\" g = g ⋆ f"}},{"Text":". The left unitor of "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)^\"op\""}},{"Text":" is the right unitor of "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)"}},{"Text":" and vice versa, and the associator of "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)^\"op\""}},{"Text":" is the inverse of the associator of "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)"}},{"Text":", with its arguments reversed."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Since the 2-cells keep their direction, a lax functor "},{"Math":{"src":"F : cal(B) ->\ncal(C)"}},{"Text":" induces a lax (not oplax) functor "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)^\"op\" ->\ncal(C)^\"op\""}},{"Text":" with the same action on cells. Reversing the 2-cells instead gives the bicategory "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)^\"co\""}},{"Text":", whose hom-categories are the opposites "},{"Math":{"src":"(cal(B) (x, y))^\"op\""}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Duality saves work: a coherence lemma about "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)"}},{"Text":" can often be obtained by instantiating a companion lemma at "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(B)^\"op\""}},{"Text":", which swaps left and right."}]}]}}}]}}
